# Entry Main. The one structural actual is opened: its fields are the actuals of the structural call, each bound to
# the input of its outer name (the reading E; step 21.7 K2). `Sum\add(Args)` with Args = (a 7, b 3) adds 73; a group
# written in the call gives its field to the input of that name, and the other input keeps its own value:
# `Sum\add((int: b 4))` adds 14. `Counter\steps` is 87.
# Norm: the book #structural-call (`C(A)` may take A whole or pass its fields -- the declaration selection decides);
# #declaration-selection.
Counter:
    int: steps 0
end: Counter
Sum:
    int: a 1
    int: b 2
    add:
        Counter\steps := Counter\steps + a * 10 + b
    end: add
end: Sum
Args:
    int: a 7
    int: b 3
end: Args
Main:
    Sum\add(Args)
    Sum\add((int: b 4))
